{"type": "text", "text": "I have everything needed. Here is the comprehensive report.

---

## Summary

The repo is at `/workspace/repo`. Note: **schedule scaffolding already exists** at `pkg/cmd/pulumi/stack/stack_schedule.go` (all subcommands are stubs returning `errors.New("not yet implemented")`, gated behind `Hidden: true` and TODO issue links). No schedule apitype or client methods exist yet.

---

### 1. Client method structure & HTTP helpers — `pkg/backend/httpstate/client/client.go`

**The `Client` struct** (line 184) holds `apiURL`, `apiToken apiAccessToken`, `diag diag.Sink`, and `restClient restClient`.

**Three wrapper helpers on `*Client`** (all delegate to `pc.restClient.Call`):

```go
// line 252
func (pc *Client) restCall(ctx context.Context, method, path string, queryObj, reqObj, respObj any) error {
	return pc.restClient.Call(ctx, pc.diag, pc.apiURL, method, path, queryObj, reqObj, respObj, pc.apiToken,
		httpCallOptions{})
}

// line 259
func (pc *Client) restCallWithOptions(
	ctx context.Context, method, path string, queryObj, reqObj,
	respObj any, opts httpCallOptions,
) error {
	return pc.restClient.Call(ctx, pc.diag, pc.apiURL, method, path, queryObj, reqObj, respObj, pc.apiToken, opts)
}

// line 269 — uses an update-lease token instead of the API token
func (pc *Client) updateRESTCall(ctx context.Context, method, path string, queryObj, reqObj, respObj any,
	token updateToken, httpOptions httpCallOptions) error
```

**Low-level interface & impl** (`api.go` lines 564–588):

```go
type restClient interface {
	HTTPClient() httpClient
	Call(ctx context.Context, diag diag.Sink, cloudAPI, method, path string, queryObj, reqObj,
		respObj any, tok accessToken, opts httpCallOptions) error
}

func (c *defaultRESTClient) Call(ctx context.Context, diag diag.Sink, cloudAPI, method, path string, queryObj, reqObj,
	respObj any, tok accessToken, opts httpCallOptions) error
```

`queryObj` is encoded via `github.com/google/go-querystring/query`; `reqObj` is JSON-marshalled (or sent verbatim if `json.RawMessage`); `respObj` accepts `**http.Response`, `*io.ReadCloser`, or a pointer for JSON decode. Use `nil` for any that don't apply.

`httpCallOptions` (`api.go` line 172) fields: `RetryPolicy`, `GzipCompress bool`, `Header http.Header`, `ErrorResponse any`, `SkipDecodeErrors bool`.

`updateAccessToken` (`api.go` line 225): `func updateAccessToken(source UpdateTokenSource) updateToken`.

**GET / POST / DELETE examples** (webhook methods, the closest analog to schedules — all use `getStackPath`):

```go
// GET (client.go:745)
func (pc *Client) ListStackWebhooks(ctx context.Context, stackID StackIdentifier) ([]apitype.Webhook, error) {
	var resp []apitype.Webhook
	if err := pc.restCall(ctx, "GET", getStackPath(stackID, "hooks"), nil, nil, &resp); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return resp, nil
}

// POST (client.go:776)
func (pc *Client) CreateStackWebhook(ctx context.Context, stackID StackIdentifier, req apitype.Webhook,
) (apitype.Webhook, error) {
	var resp apitype.Webhook
	if err := pc.restCall(ctx, "POST", getStackPath(stackID, "hooks"), nil, &req, &resp); err != nil {
		return apitype.Webhook{}, err
	}
	return resp, nil
}

// DELETE (client.go:787)
func (pc *Client) DeleteStackWebhook(ctx context.Context, stackID StackIdentifier, webhookName string) error {
	return pc.restCall(ctx, "DELETE", getStackPath(stackID, "hooks", webhookName), nil, nil, nil)
}
```

A GET with a query object: `GetStackDriftRuns` (client.go:729) passes `queryObj` as the 4th arg. A POST with a custom header via options: `CreateDeployment` (client.go:1682) uses `restCallWithOptions` with `httpCallOptions{Header: ...}`.

**Path builders** (client.go):
```go
// line 283
func getStackPath(stack StackIdentifier, components ...string) string {
	prefix := fmt.Sprintf("/api/stacks/%s/%s/%s", stack.Owner, stack.Project, stack.Stack)
	return path.Join(append([]string{prefix}, components...)...)
}

// line 1677 — deployments-scoped variant
func getDeploymentPath(stack StackIdentifier, components ...string) string {
	prefix := fmt.Sprintf("/api/stacks/%s/%s/%s/deployments", stack.Owner, stack.Project, stack.Stack)
	return path.Join(append([]string{prefix}, components...)...)
}
```
Also `getProjectPath(owner, projectName)` (line 277) and several `*Path(orgName)` helpers for policy endpoints.

**`StackIdentifier`** (`api.go` line 137):
```go
type StackIdentifier struct {
	Owner   string
	Project string
	Stack   tokens.StackName
}
func (s StackIdentifier) String() string  // "owner/project/stack"
```
Note `Stack` is a `tokens.StackName`, not a string — use `.String()` when you need the string (as `stack_webhook_new.go:332` does).

---

### 2. Files in `pkg/backend/httpstate/client/`

`ai.go`, `api.go`, `api_endpoints.go`, `client.go`, `console.go`, `doc.go`, `marshal.go` (+ their `_test.go` files, plus `client_deployments_test.go`, `client_insights_test.go`, `client_webhook_test.go`, etc.).

There is **no `endpoints.go`** for path helpers — path helpers live inline in `client.go` (the `get*Path` functions above). `api.go` holds the transport layer (`pulumiAPICall`, `defaultRESTClient`, `StackIdentifier`, token types, retry policy). `api_endpoints.go` only maps method+path → OpenTracing span names (`cleanPath`, `getEndpointName`), not URL construction.

---

### 3. apitype — `sdk/go/common/apitype/deployments.go`

Standard file structure: Apache copyright header, `package apitype`, imports:
```go
import (
	"encoding/json"
	"fmt"
	"time"
	"gopkg.in/yaml.v3"
)
```

**`CreateDeploymentRequest` already exists** at `sdk/go/common/apitype/deployments.go:102`:
```go
type CreateDeploymentRequest struct {
	Op              PulumiOperation        `json:"operation"`
	InheritSettings bool                   `json:"inheritSettings"`
	Executor        *ExecutorContext       `json:"executorContext,omitempty"`
	Source          *SourceContext         `json:"sourceContext,omitempty"`
	Operation       *OperationContext      `json:"operationContext,omitempty"`
	AgentPoolID     *AgentPoolIDMarshaller `json:"agentPoolID,omitempty"`
}
```
`PulumiOperation` (line 25) is a string type with constants `Update`, `Preview`, `Destroy`, `Refresh`, `DetectDrift`, `RemediateDrift`, plus a `ParsePulumiOperation(o string)` helper. `CreateDeploymentResponse` also lives in this file. **No schedule-related apitype exists yet** (only an unrelated `ScheduledScanEnabled` field in `insights.go`).

