### 4. `pkg/cmd/pulumi/stack/` — command structure & obtaining a client

Files: `stack.go` (parent command), plus one file per subcommand (`stack_init.go`, `stack_ls.go`, `stack_rm.go`, `stack_rename.go`, `stack_output.go`, the `stack_webhook_*.go` family, `stack_drift*.go`, and the **existing `stack_schedule.go`**), each with a matching `_test.go`.

**The helper to get an httpstate client + `StackIdentifier` is `RequireCloudStack`** (`io.go:547`):
```go
func RequireCloudStack(
	ctx context.Context, sink diag.Sink, ws pkgWorkspace.Context, lm cmdBackend.LoginManager,
	stackName string,
) (*client.Client, client.StackIdentifier, error) {
	opts := display.Options{Color: cmdutil.GetGlobalColorization()}
	s, err := RequireStack(ctx, sink, ws, lm, stackName, LoadOnly, opts)
	// ...
	cloudStack, ok := s.(httpstate.Stack)   // errors if not the Pulumi Cloud backend
	// ...
	be := cloudStack.Backend().(httpstate.Backend)
	return be.Client(), cloudStack.StackIdentifier(), nil
}
```

